HOW THE TOGGLE WORKS (already built, shared library)
----------------------------------------------------
Per-script flags at top of the script:
  USE_V8  = True   -> DATA reads (sranalytics / srlive) go to v8
  SEND_V8 = True   -> srtrade order/fill traffic goes to v8  (False = send to v7 while reading v8 data)
Wiring in the script (ORDER MATTERS):
  USE_V8 / SEND_V8 flags, then:
     if USE_V8:
         from spdr_rock_order_functions import use_v8 as _use_v8
         _use_v8(True, send=SEND_V8)
     from spdr_rock_order_functions import *      # MUST come AFTER use_v8()
  GOTCHA: `import *` copies the get_closest_* SQL strings by value. If use_v8() runs AFTER the
  import *, the script keeps the stale v7 table name. Always flip before the star-import.

Routing is by DATABASE (spdr_rock_functions.run_query -> _host_port_for):
  database == "srtrade"  -> follows SEND_V8
  everything else        -> follows USE_V8
  (so order sends AND their fill/cancel lookups stay together on the same env.)


