  is unchanged). srlive access had to be granted by SR.


SEND-SIDE CHANGES (SEND_V8)  -- order-gateway + cancel schema/enum differences
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All gated on _srf.SEND_V8 in spdr_rock_order_functions.py so v7 stays byte-identical.

1. timeInForce -> marketSession, value 'Day' -> 'RegMkt'.
   Applies to BOTH msgparentordergatewayext (complex) and msgoptordergateway (outright).
   (v7 'ExtDay' would map to 'AllDay' per SR, but we only ever send 'Day'.)

2. groupingCode + riskGroupId -> hex string "XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX" (16 hex, 4 blocks).
   Helper to_v8_id(n): mask to 63 bits so leading digit is 0-7 (v8 rejects ids that parse as
   negative). _gen_id() returns the hex string when SEND_V8, else the plain v7 int. The value's
   TYPE (str vs int) also drives SQL quoting (hex ids get quoted).
   mlegLegId LEFT AS PLAIN INT for now -- SR only required hex for groupingCode/riskGroupId; mleg
   ids were accepted as ints in the working 340 test. Revisit if a future reject points at them.

3. secKey_ts (parent-level, complex only): v7 sent 'CBOE' for SPX MLeg parents. v8's
   msgparentordergatewayext enum does NOT allow 'CBOE' (error 1265). Fix: send 'NMS' for SPX on v8.
   Line: "secKey_ts": "NMS" if (_srf.SEND_V8 or symbol == "NDXP") else "CBOE".
   (Leg secKeys mlegSecKeyN_ts were already 'NMS'; outright msgoptordergateway has no parent
   secKey_ts, only okey_ts='NMS', so the outright never hit this.)

4. progressRule (complex only): v7 'Immediate' NOT in v8 enum (error 1265). SR recommends 'None'
   as the v8 default ('AllowImmediate' also accepted). We send 'None' on v8.
   v8 progressRule enum: None, Twap, Vwap, TwapReset, VwapReset, FastReset, SlowReset, TwapAlpha,
   VwapAlpha, TwapAlphaC, VwapAlphaC, AutoComplete, AllowImmediate, Manual, SpdrPulse, IOC,
   FlashMakeTake.

5. Parent CANCEL INSERT srtrade.msgsrparentcancel (cancel_order): v8 dropped userName + timestamp_us.
   userName -> modifiedBy; drop timestamp_us; timestamp = NOW() (v8 timestamp is
   yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss.sssss). v8 columns: accnt, parentNumber, clientFirm, sysEnvironment,
   runStatus, cxlReason, altCancelId, engineName, modifiedBy, modifiedIn, timestamp.
   ALSO REQUIRED (SR-confirmed): set clientFirm='AGM'. v8 error 1105 "AccountMatches rule violated"
   comes from a blank clientFirm -- the rule keys on accnt+clientFirm. v7 had NO clientFirm column
   (it matched on userName), which is why this is brand-new in v8. The order's own
   msgsrmlegbrkrstate row shows clientFirm='AGM' for our accounts. NOTE: this error only surfaces on
   an order that did NOT fill within the 3s wait (fills skip cancel). v8 fills observed ~6s after
   send (slower than the 3s wait) -> the cancel path DOES get hit; and a failed cancel currently
   raises and kills the script even though SR may still fill the order (open risk to harden).


KEY GOTCHAS / DIAGNOSTIC TIPS
-----------------------------
- MySQL error 1265 "Data truncated for column X" = an ENUM value not in v8's allowed list. It only
  reports the FIRST bad column, so fixes surface one at a time on live sends. To find them all at
  once: query information_schema.columns COLUMN_TYPE for every enum column and compare the values
  we send against each enum's allowed set. (That is how we caught progressRule proactively.)
- MySQL error 1054 "Unknown column X" = column renamed/removed on v8 (e.g. Timeinforce, userName,
  timestamp_us).
- FILL DETECTION differs on v8 (RESOLVED for 340 legacy path): a filled order in msgsrmlegbrkrstate
  shows spdrOrderStatus='Closed' AND spdrCloseReason='Filled'. v7 code (GetParentNumber) gated
  "filled" on spdrCloseReason=='Closed', which NEVER matches v8 -> it tried to cancel an
  already-filled order. FIX (SEND_V8-gated): gate "done" on spdrOrderStatus in
  {Closed,Rejected,SendReject}. SR (Saurav) confirmed spdrOrderStatus enum =
  ('PendNew','New','PendClose','Closed','Rejected','SendReject') -- same as v7.
- FILL QUANTITY (RESOLVED for 340 legacy path): use cumSquareQty for the overall PACKAGE fill on v8,
  NOT fillQuan1 (which is a per-leg qty). SR (Saurav) said leverage cumSquareQty. Applied in
  cancel_order + _get_fill_quantity (SEND_V8-gated, else fillquan1).
- Test account: when SEND_V8 and IS_TEST, swap T.AGM* -> T.AGMV8.01 (v8 test account). PROD uses the
  real _C42 accounts as-is; confirm they are provisioned on v8 before a live prod send.
- run_query default hostname changed to None (resolves via _host_port_for). __defaults__ length is
  still 7, so the `assert len(run_query.__defaults__)==7` in the fast scripts still passes.


