POST-TRADE LOGGER (algo_trade_logger.py) -- v8 fixes (2026-08-05)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Applies to the OPTIONS scripts only (350PM_FAST, and 350PM-full / 355PM once migrated). This logger
runs AFTER trading inside a try/except, so its failures are non-fatal to the trade -- but they DROP
the row from optionsResearch.algo_trade_log. Both bugs are pure v8 side-effects of the hex groupingCode
+ v8 schema. Gated on _srf.SEND_V8 so v7 stays byte-identical. Found via the 2026-08-05 350PM_FAST
prod run (traded + filled fine; logger threw). Stock scripts do NOT use this logger -> unaffected.

1. groupingCode int() crash: v7 groupingCode was an int; the logger did int(row.groupingCode) as a dict
   key in _query_sr_fills AND _query_fill_times. v8's hex 'XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX' -> ValueError: invalid
   literal for int(). FIX: added _norm_gc(gc)=str(gc).strip().upper(), used on BOTH the map-build side
   and every consumer lookup (fill_map/fill_times in log_trades). For v7 ints _norm_gc is just str(int),
   so keys stay internally consistent -> v7 unchanged.
   LATENT 2nd half of this bug (would have silently logged 0 fills even after the int() fix): the sender
   writes groupingCode LOWERCASE ('...110d') but SR returns it UPPERCASE ('...110D'). The SQL IN(...)
   still matches (MySQL char compare is case-insensitive) but the Python dict lookups are case-sensitive.
   _norm_gc uppercasing both sides closes this too.

2. fillDttm_us dropped on v8: _query_fill_times' CASE fallback used 'fillDttm + INTERVAL fillDttm_us
   MICROSECOND'. v8's srtrade.msgsrparentexecution has NO fillDttm_us -> whole query 1054s at parse time
   (MySQL validates every column even in an unexecuted CASE branch). engTimestamp (primary branch) and
   fillDttm both still exist on v8. FIX: fallback term = 'fillDttm' on v8, full v7 expression otherwise.
   Did NOT surface in the 8/5 run because bug #1 threw first; would break the next run once #1 is fixed.

Note: _query_sr_fills reads fillQuan1 from msgsrmlegbrkrstate for the package qty -- fine on v8 for
equal-leg fills (validated: 350PM_FAST 1-lot logged size_filled=1). This is the SAME table/column the
340/350_fast legacy send path already reads; do NOT confuse with the cumSquareQty fix, which is for the
ORDER module's fill DETECTION, not this logger.
IMPLICATION FOR 350PM-full / 355PM: they call this same log_trades on v8 hex codes -> both fixes above
already cover them. No extra logger work needed when those scripts migrate.

